</figure>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS4.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Synergy of Geometric and Semantic Reconstruction Targets.</h4>

<div id="S4.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We analyze the impact of different supervision signals for the Spa3R pre-training targets. <a href="#S4.T4" title="In Synergy of Geometric and Semantic Reconstruction Targets. ‣ 4.4 Ablation Studies ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Spa3R: Predictive Spatial Field Modeling for 3D Visual Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Tab.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> compares models trained with geometric features, semantic features and linguistic features, and their combination. Results indicate that using either modality in isolation yields suboptimal performance. The best performance is achieved when combining both, suggesting that robust spatial reasoning requires both explicit geometric structure and high-level semantic context.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T4" class="ltx_table">
